  "facts": {
    "combat_persistence": "Concrete addAdditionalSaveData/readAdditionalSaveData call only their superclass with the same CompoundTag. IA-monster and Animation_Monsters declare neither override; vanilla ancestry owns health/effects/attributes/equipment and other native state. No local keys for raw attack state, attackTicks, cooldowns or presentation fields; no inherited IABoss LifeRemain or boss Home/GlobalPos/timer/bucket/self_regen persistence on this chain. Fresh/default state is not an invented generic receipt or runtime cache. The separate existing native CMWorldData IgnisDefeatedOnce flag is encounter SavedData, not per-Berserker progression or local NBT.",
    "combat_state_prerequisites": "Concrete defineSynchedData calls only the protected IA-monster superclass; no local synced shield, anger, phase, weapon, owner or progression field. Reuse ATTACK_STATE int default0 and get/setAttackState: raw input, attackTicks reset0, native synced write and byte(-state) event; no clamp or healing. IA-monster tick increments attackTicks only for positive state; these are state counters, not duration effects or automatic scalars. Constructor local sword_dance_cooldown/spin_cooldown start0; execution/reset/selection readers are deferred to R2k13b. Local AnimationState fields are presentation; no animation-only method bodies reviewed. No concrete incoming state/HP/shield gate or activation/altar prerequisite is added.",
    "death_state_reset": "Concrete die(source) invokes protected Animation_Monsters.die with the same source, then unconditionally setAttackState(0) when the void super call returns normally. Existing native CommonHooks death cancellation/removed/dead/source-credit gates remain in super; even an early canceled return does not suppress this concrete state reset. Inherited raw setter also resets attackTicks and broadcasts native byte0. Concrete deathtimer returns20, retaining the existing IA/common native death-duration boundary. No extra concrete heal, hurt, phase immunity, respawner, world-flag write or offensive payload is present in these methods. Full offensive/death/terrain callback closure remains R2k13b.",
    "encounter_setup": "Exact ModEntities factory lambda$static$23 bootstrap90 constructs Ignited_Berserker; ID binding bootstrap137 is ignited_berserker, categoryMONSTER, fireImmune, size1 x float2.4. Locked initializeAttributes binding133..149 installs follow20, speedfloat.32, attack7.5, maxHP65, armor8, step1.25, KBR1. Constructor does not call setConfigattribute or heal, does not seed boss Home/shield/anger/phase, and has no concrete finalizeSpawn/mobInteract override. Installed common config has no Berserker combat block; do not borrow Revenant multipliers. This is native attribute/type setup, not an outgoing damage request, resource gain or new encounter activation. Exhaustive global spawn/acquisition discovery is not claimed.",
    "environment_admission": "Exact registered type is fireImmune; native IS_FIRE admission/hooks remain authoritative. Concrete decreaseAirSupply returns its supplied air unchanged, not max air; it adds no blanket rejection of all drowning/custom sources in hurt. canBePushedByEntity and canRide returnfalse. Ordinary collision admission is distinct from knockback resistance1 and from custom forced movement; no claim of all-motion immunity. No concrete fluid/fall-damage/invulnerability overrides are declared. Constructor path malus rail0 and water-1 remain native navigation state. Any offense-related motion/state readers are deferred.",
    "incoming_admission": "Exact hierarchy: Berserker -> Internal_Animation_Monster -> Animation_Monsters -> native Monster. None of those three Cataclysm classes declares hurt or isInvulnerableTo. Incoming damage therefore reaches patched native LivingEntity.hurt, with existing global/status hooks intact, rather than IABoss_monster or LLibrary_Boss_Monster. Native virtual invulnerability, client/dead/fire-resistance rejection, DamageContainer/incoming event, shield/freezing/helmet processing, cooldown/actuallyHurt defenses and source/impact/totem/death/effect callbacks retain their existing order. No concrete amount rewrite, range/bucket check, direct/causing-entity substitution or post-hurt state write. True hurt still does not prove final HP loss.",
    "native_invulnerability": "Reuse Entity.isInvulnerableTo: native removed state; invulnerable flag except BYPASSES_INVULNERABILITY/creative-player source; IS_FIRE with registered fire immunity; IS_FALL with the recipient type FALL_DAMAGE_IMMUNE tag; then CommonHooks.isEntityInvulnerableTo can modify the native result. No Berserker/IA-monster/common Animation_Monsters override, phase or shield prefilter. BYPASSES_INVULNERABILITY is not a new unconditional bypass of removed/fire/type/hook admission or native cooldown/armor, whose separate tags/hooks remain native. No unconditional fall immunity or whole-source immunity is inferred from the fireImmune factory.",
    "shared_defense_applicability": "DamageCap/DpsCap/RangeLimit/NatureRegen/HealCooldown and boss Home/return bookkeeping are not on this native hierarchy. There are no concrete or IA-monster/common Animation_Monsters bindings for them. Record N/A, not Float/Double.MAX_VALUE or regen0/default timers from unrelated boss bases. No Cataclysm boss per-hit cap, DPS bucket, causing-distance falloff, self_regen reset or natural-heal delivery is introduced here. Cataclysm bypasses_hurt_time/block_self_regen do not gain those absent shared consumers; native vanilla tag membership still controls any native downstream behavior. The boss effective_for_bosses whitelist also is not inherited: existing native/global effect admission remains authoritative, not an all-effects-admitted guarantee. Native armor and knockback resistance remain distinct attributes.",
    "spawn_prerequisites": "Concrete instance checkSpawnRules first calls rollSpawn(1,random,reason). That helper returns true immediately for native isSpawner reasons; otherwise bound1 draws nextInt(1)==0, so it has no probabilistic exclusion here, but still consumes RNG. Instance next requires worldIn instanceof ServerLevel; reads CMWorldData.get(that level,Level.NETHER), requires non-null data and isIgnisDefeatedOnce true. It does not call super.checkSpawnRules or compare the current spawn dimension with NETHER; locked get resolves requested Nether SavedData with overworld fallback if unavailable. Spawner only bypasses rollSpawn RNG, not the instance world/flag gate. Separate registry placement is ON_GROUND/MOTION_BLOCKING_NO_LEAVES, REPLACE, native Monster.checkAnyLightMonsterSpawnRules. Preserve those distinct checks/native loader hooks; constructor/factory creation itself does not invoke this instance method. No new flag reset/write, boss Home seed, arena marker or universal all-spawn gate is inferred."
  },
